# Frank House Dashboard — SMS Consent Form

_This page documents the opt-in (consent) flow for the Frank House Dashboard SMS notification
service. It is the publicly viewable Call-to-Action / consent artifact for A2P 10DLC registration._

---

## Program

**Frank House Dashboard** is a private, personal home-automation notification service operated by an
individual (sole proprietor) for their own household. Participants are the account owner and their
immediate family members.

## How to opt in

Participation is **voluntary** and is **not required** to use the home dashboard. To opt in, a
participant takes this action themselves:

> ☐ **I agree to receive SMS text messages from Frank House Dashboard.**
> _(This box is unchecked by default. Checking it / opting in is optional and voluntary.)_

A participant opts in by **texting the keyword `START`** from their own mobile phone to the Frank
House Dashboard number, **or** by checking the optional consent box above when the account owner sets
up their phone for the household service. The participant's own action (texting START, or checking
the box) is the opt-in event.

## What you receive after opting in

- An SMS **confirmation reply** each time you send a note to the dashboard.
- **Message frequency varies** (typically a few messages per month).
- **Message and data rates may apply.**

## Opting out

- Reply **STOP** at any time to unsubscribe and receive no further messages.
- Reply **HELP** for help.

## Disclosures

- Messages are transactional confirmations only. **No marketing or promotional messages** are sent.
- **No mobile information is shared with any third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional
  purposes.**
- Recipients are limited to the account owner and their opted-in family members. No third parties are
  messaged.

